  "summary": "Sputnik-era design of orbiting shapes: globes, pods, bulbous forms and white plastics imagining the everyday future.",
  "description": "After Sputnik (1957), designers cast furniture, radios, lamps and interiors as spacecraft: Eero Aarnio Ball and Bubble chairs, Verner Panton environments, Olivetti's plastic computers, Populuxe radios. Molded plastic and fiberglass enabled seamless capsules; color went white-silver with orange accents. It declined with the 1970s oil crisis but remains the stock image of retrofuturism.",
